# You're Leaving Revenue on the Table With No Partner Channel

Agencies and resellers who could sell on your behalf have no program to join.

Many businesses could grow faster through agencies, consultants, or resellers who already have the customer relationships, but without a formal partner program, tiers, and enablement materials, that channel simply never gets built.

Symptoms:
- Agencies or consultants asking if you have a partner or referral program
- No formal process for tracking partner-sourced revenue
- Interested resellers with no clear onboarding path
- Revenue that could come through partners instead relying entirely on direct sales

Our solution: We help design a partner program with clear tiers, economics, and enablement materials, along with the tracking needed to attribute partner-sourced revenue, so the channel can be built deliberately instead of left informal.

FAQs:

Q: Do we need white-label capability to start a partner program?
A: No, a referral or reseller tier can launch without white-labeling; white-label is typically a later, higher tier for partners wanting full branding control.

Q: How do we track partner-sourced revenue?
A: Referral codes or links tied into your CRM allow revenue to be attributed back to the introducing partner from first touch through to close.